LU5400 CM11 RIL transport
=======================

rild is built from the existing CM11 hardware/ril/rild source. This directory
builds libril; BOARD_PROVIDES_LIBRIL prevents the platform copy from colliding.
The LG modem implementation remains the unmodified LU540141 lge-ril.so.

ril.cpp/ril_event.cpp are based on the local CM11 libril implementation.
Common platform sources are not edited. Preserve CM11's standard request
version fallbacks and framework output format, rather than copying an ICS
framework wire format unchanged.

Stock reference: LU540141 libril.so, SHA-256
add230345c2400a52d1feef31b5c2276957c60a929ff9cadbede48dc7de97133.
ELF request table: 0xa6a8, 364 entries; unsolicited: 0xa014, 95 entries.
Private entries are mapped by handler address, not guessed from P940 names.
The LU5400 LgeCall ABI has a 32-bit isVoice at offset 16, number at 24,
name at 32 and UUS pointer at 40. It is not the standard RIL_Call layout.
lu5400_compat.inc reconstructs the private integer/string payload layouts.
The lifetime of heap-backed private arguments follows stock; ownership beyond
the callback has not been established. Do not introduce early frees without
checking the modem-side consumers.

The device Java class retains its configured P2RIL name but no longer sends
P940 call-path/hangup/bootstrap requests or treats HDR_SMPS_CHANGED (1060)
as a SIM event. Unimplemented private unsolicited events are logged; their
higher-level semantics remain outside the current implementation.

CM11 adds its newer signal fields and IMS application index to old responses,
and expects a UTF-16 caller name rather than stock's byte array. Non-ASCII
caller-name encoding and unimplemented private OEM notification semantics
still require device-specific verification.

Standard request differences: GET_IMSI (11) ignores the optional AID; data
call deactivation (41) converts CM11 decimal strings to the stock int pair.
DTMF_START (49), not manual network selection (47), uses a string/int pair
in the stock native table. REA decompilation of lge-ril.so requestDtmfStart
confirms a negative second value selects AT$LGDTMF=<key> without the optional
argument. CM11's key-only input maps to -1; explicit legacy values are retained.
The key-only path is compared synthetically with stock's key/-1 input. No tone
commands were sent to the modem, and in-call DTMF remains untested.
